  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Starting a session",
      "items": [
        "1–2: the phone sends a request signed with its Keystore key; the edge forwards it and virtroidd checks the account and its credit",
        "3–4: the provisioner reuses the account's VM, takes a warm spare, or creates an SEV-SNP VM, and unlocks its disk only after its attestation matches an approved image",
        "5: the VM boots the measured, read-only image; each session starts a fresh Android container",
        "6: the phone verifies the attestation against AMD's root and the offline-signed image list, then streams straight from the VM over QUIC, or through the edge",
        "7: data is restored from Sia before Android boots and saved back, encrypted, when it stops"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "When you close the viewer",
      "items": [
        "The runtime keeps running for the period you chose, 30 minutes to a week",
        "Notifications reach your phone: app, time and title only, end-to-end encrypted",
        "Then Android stops, its data is encrypted and sharded to Sia, and the VM is destroyed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Your data",
      "items": [
        "Nothing on the phone: only non-exportable keys and an encrypted vault",
        "Encrypted inside the VM with your account key, which your identity password unlocks",
        "30 shards on independent Sia hosts; any 10 rebuild it; indexd sees only opaque metadata"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Placement",
      "items": [
        "Each account has a region; its VM is never shared",
        "Near you: a dedicated SEV-SNP server, for example in Singapore",
        "Europe and the US: Aleph Cloud's SEV-SNP hosts, paid per hour in credits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Control plane",
      "items": [
        "Edge, control, payments and storage are isolated from each other",
        "Only the edge is public; VMs and their agents also come in through it",
        "Falco, Suricata and auditd ship events off-host to an append-only bucket"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Money",
      "items": [
        "Each account deposits USDT (TRC20) to its own address",
        "The balance pays per hour a runtime runs and per GB stored",
        "Payments sweeps deposits and swaps them: Siacoin for the indexer, ETH that buys Aleph credits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Apps",
      "items": [
        "The catalogue follows F-Droid's signed index; every APK is pinned by SHA-256",
        "Each runtime has its own apps, installed once; F-Droid on it can install more"
      ]
    }
  ]
